From: Brad Nicholas <70774+bradn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:57:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Build the rendering engine for iOS; add a UIKit reading
 surface

Phase 1 and 2 of IOS-PORT-PLAN.md.

- Package.swift declares iOS 17. MarkdownRender's engine, fragments and
  themes name platform types through Platform/Platform.swift (the AppKit
  classes on macOS); the AppKit view layer compiles out on iOS.
- UIKitView/MarkdownReaderView: a read-only UITextView on TextKit 2 built
  from the same content storage, display map, decoration engine and
  fragments as MarkdownTextView, with outline, rotors, links, footnotes,
  code copy, find support and its own scroll height.
- Shared with the Mac view: Engine/PresentationMaps (moved verbatim out of
  MarkdownTextView), CodeBlockFragment.codeText, FragmentBase.columnOrigin.
- Mac-visible fix: replayed decoration programs now style whole
  paragraphs, so list items keep their spacing after re-decoration
  (DecorationReplayTests).
- Scripts/check-ios.sh builds for iOS devices and runs MarkdownCore and
  MarkdownRender tests on a simulator, then the iOS app's tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
